Passage: DIR, Art. 1(2)

[0] Article 1 Scope.
[1] 2.
[2] The following are excluded from the scope of this Directive:
[3] (a) safety components intended to be used as spare parts to replace identical components and supplied by the manufacturer of the original machinery;
[4] (b) specific equipment for use in fairgrounds and/or amusement parks;
[5] (c) machinery specially designed or put into service for nuclear purposes which, in the event of failure, may result in an emission of radioactivity;
[6] (d) weapons, including firearms;
[7] (e) the following means of transport: — agricultural and forestry tractors for the risks covered by Directive 2003/37/EC, with the exclusion of machinery mounted on these vehicles, — motor vehicles and their trailers covered by Council Directive 70/156/EEC of 6 February 1970 on the approximation of the laws of the Member States relating to the type-approval of motor vehicles and their trailers ( 13 ) , with the exclusion of machinery mounted on these vehicles, — vehicles covered by Directive 2002/24/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 March 2002 relating to the type-approval of two or three-wheel motor vehicles ( 14 ) , with the exclusion of machinery mounted on these vehicles, — motor vehicles exclusively intended for competition, and — means of transport by air, on water and on rail networks with the exclusion of machinery mounted on these means of transport;
[8] (f) seagoing vessels and mobile offshore units and machinery installed on board such vessels and/or units;
[9] (g) machinery specially designed and constructed for military or police purposes;
[10] (h) machinery specially designed and constructed for research purposes for temporary use in laboratories;
[11] (i) mine winding gear;
[12] (j) machinery intended to move performers during artistic performances;
[13] (k) electrical and electronic products falling within the following areas, insofar as they are covered by Council Directive 73/23/EEC of 19 February 1973 on the harmonisation of the laws of Member States relating to electrical equipment designed for use within certain voltage limits ( 15 ) : — household appliances intended for domestic use, — audio and video equipment, — information technology equipment, — ordinary office machinery, — low-voltage switchgear and control gear, — electric motors;
[14] (l) the following types of high-voltage electrical equipment: — switch gear and control gear, — transformers.
